## AIDA Workflow

### Commands (invoke via `/command`)

| Command | When |
|---------|------|
| `/progress` | Check status + metrics, route to next action |
| `/plan-phase N` | Research + create detailed plan for phase |
| `/execute` | Run current approved plan |
| `/verify` | Run the full verification suite |
| `/handoff [save\|resume]` | Pause with a handoff, or resume a prior session |
| `/issues [add\|review]` | Log a deferred issue, or triage the backlog |

### Subagents

| Agent | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| researcher | Gather context before planning |
| planner | Create PLAN.md (with acceptance criteria + verify commands) |
| executor | Execute plan segments; stages work, does NOT commit |
| test-writer-fixer | Independent watchdog: makes tests real, flags product bugs |
| reviewer | Verify + audit, log escapes, mark APPROVED |

### Mandatory AIDA Sequence

> Every implementation task MUST follow this sequence. No exceptions.

```
researcher -> planner -> (user approval) -> commit plan -> executor -> test-writer-fixer -> reviewer -> (commit on APPROVE)
```

After user approval and before spawning the first executor, the orchestrator commits PLAN.md and planning artifacts. **The executor and watchdog STAGE their work but do NOT commit** — the commit happens only after the reviewer marks `APPROVED` (enforced by the review-before-commit hook). This makes the reviewed unit equal the committed unit.

### State Files

```
.planning/
├── PROJECT.md    # What we're building
├── ROADMAP.md    # Phase breakdown
├── STATE.md      # Current position (READ THIS FIRST)
├── ISSUES.md     # Deferred work
├── ESCAPES.md    # Escape catalog — known failure patterns (grows over time)
├── WIP.md        # Work-in-progress (auto-updated during execution)
└── phases/XX-name/
    ├── PLAN.md            # Phase plan (committed before execution)
    ├── SUMMARY-XX.Y.md    # Per-segment summaries (written by executor)
    ├── WATCHDOG-XX.Y.md   # Watchdog test findings (written by test-writer-fixer)
    └── SUMMARY.md         # Phase summary (written by reviewer)
```

### Enforcement (hooks)

AIDA ships hooks that enforce the pipeline — they are not advisory:

- **Review-before-commit gate** — a `git commit` that touches code is **blocked** unless `STATE.md` contains `Commit-Gate: APPROVED`. The reviewer sets this on APPROVE; the executor resets it to `LOCKED` when a segment starts. Commits that only touch `.planning/` files (plans, state) are always allowed.
- **Escape-before-commit gate** — if `STATE.md` has `Escape-Pending: yes` (a post-review fix was made), commits are blocked until the escape is logged in `ESCAPES.md` and the flag cleared.
- **Session-start / prompt-context / stop** — surface WIP on resume, inject current position each turn, and remind you to checkpoint uncommitted work.

Keep the `Commit-Gate:` and `Escape-Pending:` lines in `STATE.md` in `Key: Value` form at the start of a line — the hooks match them literally. The gate is **opt-in**: it only enforces once a `Commit-Gate:` line is present (a project without it commits normally).

